# Lion's Eye Diamond's mana ability is activated only as an instant, so never while a spell is being cast (its ruling, CR
# 601.2g, 605.3a), unlike Lotus Petal's. With Uro, Titan of Nature's Wrath and two other cards in the graveyard and two
# Islands in hand, the Diamond's "Discard your hand, Sacrifice this artifact" would make five other cards, but it can't be
# activated while Uro is cast by escape (CR 702.138a), so the escape is not offered - with mana to spare or not. Activated at
# priority first, the hand and the Diamond are in the graveyard and its {U}{U}{U} floats beside Black Lotus's {G}{G}{G}: the
# escape is then offered, paid and exiles all five.

